  "id": "COMPOUND:23663 - PROTEIN:6318",
  "verbalization": "Phellandral, (R)- is implicated in the regulation of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10 through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Phellandral, (R)- acts as a target for several compounds, which in turn target UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10. Specifically, Phellandral, (R)- is directly linked to UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B15, which is a target of Marlignan J, and Marlignan J further targets UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10. This indicates a potential pathway where Phellandral, (R)- may influence the activity of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10 through its interaction with Marlignan J. Additionally, Phellandral, (R)- is also linked to CDK3/Cyclin E, which is a target of Urs-20-en-3-yl acetate and Z-senegasaponin a, both of which also target UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10. These findings suggest that Phellandral, (R)- may exert its effects on UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10 through a complex network of molecular interactions, potentially involving enzyme inhibition or regulatory modulation. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Phellandral, (R)- and UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
